{% comment %}
  InstaMom University — "What's inside" disclosure for an ADD-ON.

  Owner review: "Some add-ons need to be clickable to list what they actually
  include — Extra Snack Sleeve packs, laundry rescue packs. For now it would be
  fine to just list the same three dummy items for each and we can change in
  later."

  Data source, in order:
   1. The add-on's own `custom.whats_inside` metafield (the same list metafield
      the packages use — see the run-shopify-store skill). Set that and the real
      contents appear here with no theme change.
   2. Otherwise, the placeholder below, but ONLY for the add-ons the review
      named. That keeps the disclosure off the self-explanatory extras (a roll
      of toilet paper doesn't need a contents list).

  Rendered as a <details> disclosure rather than a nested modal on purpose: this
  appears INSIDE the add-ons modal, and opening a dialog on top of a dialog
  traps focus and can't be dismissed cleanly.

  Usage: {% render 'instamom-addon-contents', addon: addon %}
  Styling: .instamom-addon-contents* in assets/instamom.css
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign items = addon.metafields.custom.whats_inside.value

  # Handles the review called out. Drop a handle from this list once its real
  # `custom.whats_inside` metafield is filled in — the metafield wins anyway.
  assign placeholder_handles = 'addon-snacks-chips,addon-snacks-cookies,addon-laundry,addon-athlete-recovery' | split: ','
  assign use_placeholder = false
  if items == blank
    for handle in placeholder_handles
      if addon.handle == handle
        assign use_placeholder = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if items != blank and items.size > 0 -%}
  <details class="instamom-addon-contents">
    <summary class="instamom-addon-contents__toggle">What&rsquo;s inside</summary>
    <ul class="instamom-addon-contents__list">
      {%- for item in items -%}<li>{{ item }}</li>{%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </details>
{%- elsif use_placeholder -%}
  <details class="instamom-addon-contents">
    <summary class="instamom-addon-contents__toggle">What&rsquo;s inside</summary>
    <ul class="instamom-addon-contents__list">
      <li>Sample item one</li>
      <li>Sample item two</li>
      <li>Sample item three</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="instamom-addon-contents__todo">Placeholder contents &mdash; to be replaced.</p>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
